Common Follow-Up Questions
“Why did you use two Lookup activities?”

The first Lookup retrieved the last successful watermark from the control table. The second Lookup retrieved the current maximum Modified Timestamp from the source table. The Copy Activity used these two values to extract a stable incremental range.

“Why did you use Batch ID?”

The watermark identified which source records to extract, while the Batch ID tracked those extracted records through Landing, Bronze, Silver, Gold, Synapse, and audit tables. This gave us end-to-end traceability and controlled restart capability.

“Why did you use Parquet in Landing?”

Parquet is a columnar format that preserves datatypes, reduces storage through compression, and provides better read performance for Databricks and Synapse compared with CSV.

“Why did you use Bronze if the source was already Parquet?”

Landing preserved the extracted files, while Bronze converted the batch into a managed Delta table with audit metadata, ACID support, schema enforcement, history, and reliable downstream processing.

“How did you handle invalid records?”

We created Boolean validation flags after transformation. Blocking failures were written to a rejection-reasons array and routed to quarantine. Optional issues were classified as warnings, allowing the record to continue as accepted with warning.

“How did you handle failures?”

Every major ADF activity had a failure path that updated the audit table, captured the failed stage and error message, sent an alert, and failed the pipeline. Persisted layers allowed us to restart from Landing, Bronze, Silver, Gold, or Synapse without repeating successful stages.

“When did you update the watermark?”

We updated the watermark only after the final Synapse load and reconciliation succeeded. If any stage failed, the previous successful watermark remained unchanged.

“What was your role?”

My responsibilities included developing parameterized ADF pipelines, implementing watermark-based incremental ingestion, creating PySpark transformation and validation logic, building Bronze and Silver Delta tables, implementing Delta MERGE, handling quarantine records, performing reconciliation, integrating Gold outputs with Synapse staging, and supporting pipeline monitoring and failure recovery.

